    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Long Branch Historic House & Farm, built around 1811, spans 400 acres and is maintained by the nonprofit Historic Long Branch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://experienceclarkecounty.com/directory-attractions/listing/long-branch-historical-house-farm/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Named a Virginia Historic Landmark in 1968, Long Branch entered the National Register of Historic Places the following year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlongbranch.org/history-1",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1788, Robert Carter Burwell inherited the Long Branch land and began a wheat plantation worked by enslaved people.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlongbranch.org/history-1",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Around 1810, Burwell commissioned a Federal‑style mansion and sought design advice from architect Benjamin Henry Latrobe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlongbranch.org/history-1",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After Burwell’s 1813 death, the Nelsons operated Long Branch as a girls’ school during the 1830s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlongbranch.org/history-1",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In the 1840s, Hugh Mortimer Nelson transformed the house with Greek Revival renovations, adding a spiral staircase and columned porticos.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
